  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a **0-indexed** `m x n` integer matrix `grid`. The width of a column is the largest **length** of its integers.\n\n* As an example, if `grid = [[-10], [3], [12]]`, the width of the only column is `3` since `-10` is of length `3`.\n\nOutput *an integer array* `ans` *of size* `n` *where* `ans[i]` *is the width of the* `ith` *column*.\n\nThe **length** of an integer `x` with `len` digits is equal to `len` if `x` is non-negative, and `len + 1` otherwise.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: grid = [[1],[22],[333]]\nOutput: [3]\nExplanation: In the 0th column, 333 is of length 3.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: grid = [[-15,1,3],[15,7,12],[5,6,-2]]\nOutput: [3,1,2]\nExplanation: \nIn the 0th column, only -15 is of length 3.\nIn the 1st column, all integers are of length 1. \nIn the 2nd column, both 12 and -2 are of length 2.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `m == grid.length`\n* `n == grid[i].length`\n* `1 <= m, n <= 100`\n* `-109 <= grid[r][c] <= 109`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
